{{define "apps.gohtml"}}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>School ERP — staff apps</title>
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/app.css?v={{.AssetVersion}}">
{{template "themeboot"}}
</head>
<body class="marketing apps">

<header class="topbar">
  <span class="wordmark">School ERP</span>
  <span class="spacer"></span>
  {{template "themebtn"}}
  <a class="quiet" href="/login">Sign in</a>
</header>

<main>
  <section class="apps-hero">
    <h1>Staff apps for Android</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Two apps run on school handsets rather than in a browser. They are not on
      Google Play yet, so they are installed from here. Open this page
      <strong>on the phone the app will live on</strong> and tap Download.
    </p>
  </section>

  {{if not .AnyAvailable}}
  <p class="apps-none" role="status">
    No build has been published to this server yet. Nothing to install today —
    check back, or ask the school's supplier.
  </p>
  {{end}}

  <section class="apps-list" aria-label="Available apps">
    {{range .Apps}}
    <article class="app-card{{if not .Available}} unbuilt{{end}}">
      <div class="app-head">
        <h2>{{.Name}}</h2>
        {{if .Available}}<span class="app-version">v{{.Version}}</span>{{end}}
      </div>
      <p class="app-tagline">{{.Tagline}}</p>

      <p class="app-who"><span class="app-label">Goes on</span> {{.Who}}</p>
      <ul class="app-needs">
        {{range .Needs}}<li>{{.}}</li>{{end}}
      </ul>

      {{if .Available}}
      <a class="app-dl" href="/apps/{{.Slug}}.apk" rel="nofollow">
        Download {{.Size}}
      </a>
      <dl class="app-facts">
        <dt>Built</dt><dd>{{.Built}}</dd>
        <dt>File</dt><dd>{{.File}}</dd>
        {{if .SHA256}}<dt>SHA-256</dt><dd class="app-sum">{{.SHA256}}</dd>{{end}}
      </dl>
      {{else}}
      <p class="app-pending">Not published to this server yet.</p>
      {{end}}
    </article>
    {{end}}
  </section>

  <section class="apps-howto">
    <h2>Installing it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Tap <strong>Download</strong> above on the phone itself.</li>
      <li>Open the downloaded file. Android will say it cannot install apps from
          this source — that is expected, and it says it for everything that did
          not come from Play.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Settings</strong> on that message and turn on
          <strong>Allow from this source</strong> for your browser. Turn it back
          off afterwards if you like; the app keeps working.</li>
      <li>Go back and tap <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
      <li>Open the app. It will ask for a <strong>pair code</strong>.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="pairing">The pair code</h2>
    <p>
      Neither app does anything at all until it is paired. An administrator
      generates an eight-character code in the school's console — SMS gateway or
      transport screen — and it expires in ten minutes. Type it into the handset
      within that window and the phone is joined to that school and no other.
    </p>
    <p class="apps-note">
      That is why this page needs no password. The file on its own is inert: it
      cannot reach any school's data without a code an administrator issued.
      Guard the code, not the download.
    </p>

    <h2>Checking what you downloaded</h2>
    <p>
      Sideloaded apps get no store check on the way in, so the SHA-256 above is
      the only proof the file is ours. Anyone who wants to verify it can, on a
      computer:
    </p>
    <pre class="apps-code">sha256sum bus-tracker-1.0.0.apk</pre>
    <p>
      If it does not match the figure on this page character for character, do
      not install it.
    </p>

    <h2>When these reach Google Play</h2>
    <p>
      This page stays. A school that has already installed from here keeps
      working, and Play becomes the easier of two routes rather than a migration
      anyone has to perform.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>

{{template "themejs"}}
</body>
</html>{{end}}
